> Is this right? "the share of population within a bin who experience damages"
> Or is it "experiences"?
**assistant**:
> Use **“experience”**:
> 
> > “the share of population within a bin who experience damages”
> 
> The verb agrees with **“who”** referring to the people in the population, not with “share.” Even smoother:
> 
> > “the share of the population within a bin that experiences damages.”
